\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-360\li720\tx720\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.\tab O GOD of our forefathers, hear,
\par \pard\li720 And make Thy faithful mercies known ;
\par To Thee through Jesus we draw near,
\par Thy suffering, well-beloved Son,
\par In whom Thy smiling face we see,
\par In whom Thou art well pleased with me.
\par \pard 
\par \pard\fi-360\li720\tx720\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2.\tab With solemn faith we offer up,
\par \pard\li720 And spread before Thy glorious eyes,
\par That only ground of all our hope,
\par That precious, bleeding sacrifice,
\par Which brings Thy grace on sinners down,
\par And perfects all our souls in one.
\par \pard 
\par \pard\fi-360\li720\tx720\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3.\tab Acceptance through His only name ,
\par \pard\li720 Forgiveness in His blood, we have ;
\par But more abundant life we claim
\par Through Him who died our souls to save,
\par To sanctify us by his blood,
\par And fill with all the life of God.
\par \pard 
\par \pard\fi-360\li720\tx720\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4.\tab Father, behold Thy dying son,
\par \pard\li720 And hear the blood that speaks above ,
\par On us let all Thy grace be shown,
\par Peace, righteousness, and joy, and love,
\par Thy kingdom come to every heart,
\par And all Thou hast, and all Thou art.
\par Amen.
\par \pard\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs16 
\par }

